  "worked_solution": "First, note that the range of $\\theta =\\operatorname{arcsin}\u2061x$ is given by\n\n$$\n-{90}^{\u2218}\\le \\theta \\le {90}^{\u2218}.\n$$\n\nNote that the angle $\\theta $ spans the first and fourth quadrants.\n\nSince $\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}$ is positive, our answer is an angle that lies in the first quadrant, where sine is positive.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14036892/assets/d93c490adbb5cdbc0e9a09b60eea9b82ab93be8e871e334423abc17ddd62955e.png)\n\nFrom the values in the first quadrant, we see that\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{sin}\u2061({45}^{\u2218})=\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{arcsin}\u2061(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})={45}^{\u2218}.\n$$",
